{"scope":"jinshu/032 native witness-binding reproducers; projected contract fields only; no chronology/content approval","graphs":[{"personId":"jinshu:032:p022","witness":{"localId":"jinshu:032:p022","book":"jinshu","chapter":"032","unitId":"s0044","quote":"成恭杜皇后諱陵陽[2]，京兆人，鎮南將軍預之曾孫也。"},"baselinePass":false,"error":"Witness does not support this person in the current primary source: jinshu:032:p022 jinshu:032:s0044 quote=\"成恭杜皇后諱陵陽[2]，京兆人，鎮南將軍預之曾孫也。\""},{"personId":"jinshu:032:p029","witness":{"localId":"jinshu:032:p029","book":"jinshu","chapter":"032","unitId":"s0063","quote":"裴氏名穆，長水校尉綽孫，太傅主簿遐女，太尉王夷甫外孫。"},"baselinePass":false,"error":"Witness does not support this person in the current primary source: jinshu:032:p029 jinshu:032:s0063 quote=\"裴氏名穆，長水校尉綽孫，太傅主簿遐女，太尉王夷甫外孫。\""},{"personId":"jinshu:032:p094","witness":{"localId":"jinshu:032:p094","book":"jinshu","chapter":"032","unitId":"s0191","quote":"先適渤海田氏，生一男而寡，依于舅濮陽吳氏。"},"baselinePass":false,"error":"Witness does not support this person in the current primary source: jinshu:032:p094 jinshu:032:s0191 quote=\"先適渤海田氏，生一男而寡，依于舅濮陽吳氏。\""},{"personId":"jinshu:032:p157","witness":{"localId":"jinshu:032:p157","book":"jinshu","chapter":"032","unitId":"s0272","quote":"是以塗山作儷，而夏族以熙；"},"baselinePass":false,"error":"Witness does not support this person in the current primary source: jinshu:032:p157 jinshu:032:s0272 quote=\"是以塗山作儷，而夏族以熙；\""},{"personId":"jinshu:032:p049","witness":{"localId":"jinshu:032:p049","book":"jinshu","chapter":"032","unitId":"s0314","quote":"贊曰：二妃光舜，三母翼周。"},"baselinePass":true,"error":null}],"units":[{"id":"s0044","zh":"成恭杜皇后諱陵陽[2]，京兆人，鎮南將軍預之曾孫也。","en":"Empress Du's personal name was Lingyang; she came from Jingzhao and was the great-granddaughter of Du Yu, General Who Guards the South.","literal":"Empress Du the Chenggong had the taboo personal name Lingyang; she was a person of Jingzhao and was the great-granddaughter of the General Who Guards the South, Yu."},{"id":"s0045","zh":"父乂，見《外戚傳》。","en":"Her father was Du Yi; see the outer-kin biographies.","literal":"Her father was Yi; see the 'Biographies of the Outer Relations.'"},{"id":"s0063","zh":"裴氏名穆，長水校尉綽孫，太傅主簿遐女，太尉王夷甫外孫。","en":"Lady Pei was named Mu—granddaughter of the Colonel of the Chang River Guard Pei Chuo, daughter of the Grand Tutor's registrar Pei Xia, and maternal granddaughter of Grand Commandant Wang Yifu.","literal":"The Lady Pei had the name Mu; she was granddaughter of the Colonel of the Chang River Guard Chuo, daughter of the Registrar of the Grand Tutor Xia, and maternal granddaughter of Grand Commandant Wang Yifu."},{"id":"s0087","zh":"伏惟陛下德侔二媯，淑美關雎，臨朝攝政，以寧天下。","en":"We believe your virtue rivals the two wives of Shun, your grace recalls the \"Guanju\" ode—take the reins of government and calm the empire.","literal":"We humbly consider that Your Majesty's virtue matches the two Gui; good and beautiful as 'Guanju'; attend court and hold the regency, thereby to bring peace to all under Heaven."},{"id":"s0190","zh":"后少孤，無兄弟，唯姊妹四人，后最長。","en":"Orphaned young, she had no brothers—only four sisters, of whom she was the eldest.","literal":"The empress in youth was orphaned; she had no brothers; only four sisters; the empress was eldest."},{"id":"s0191","zh":"先適渤海田氏，生一男而寡，依于舅濮陽吳氏。","en":"She had married into the Tian family of Bohai, borne a son, and been widowed; she then lived under the protection of her maternal uncle, the Wu clan of Puyang.","literal":"First she married into the Tian clan of Bohai; bearing one boy she became a widow and relied on her maternal uncle's Wu clan of Puyang."},{"id":"s0272","zh":"是以塗山作儷，而夏族以熙；","en":"The lady of Tushan wed Yu and the Xia flourished;","literal":"Therefore Tushan became mate and Xia clan thereby prospered;"},{"id":"s0314","zh":"贊曰：二妃光舜，三母翼周。","en":"The encomium reads: Two royal wives brought glory to Shun; three nurturing mothers bore Zhou aloft.","literal":"Encomium says: Two consorts illumined Shun; three mothers winged Zhou."}],"people":[{"localId":"jins